Approach 1: Direct Mutation (Failed)
Emission: INSERT into signals table
Retraction: UPDATE signals table SET retracted = true WHERE id = X
  Approach 2: Soft Delete with Tombstones (Failed)
Emission: INSERT into signals table (status = 'active')
Retraction: INSERT into signals table (status = 'retraction', references original)
Feature store: SELECT ... WHERE status = 'active'
  Approach 3: Event Log + Materialized View (What We Actually Built)
Event log: APPEND-ONLY. Every emission and every retraction is an event.
           Events have a logical timestamp (not wall clock — sequence number).
           No mutations, no deletes, no updates. Ever.

Materialized view: Rebuilt from the event log. Contains the CURRENT state
                   of every signal (active or retracted). This is what the
                   feature store reads from.

Reconciliation: Periodic job that compares the materialized view to the
                event log. If they disagree, the event log wins.
